writerFailed=["The headline is not much bigger than the text under it.", "The eye does not land on the headline first.", "More than one button competes as the main action.", "The main button sits low on the screen.", "The navigation is as loud as the headline.", "Too many items shout for attention at once.", "Some text is hard to read against its background.", "Several text items are too faint against their background.", "The faintest text is too faint against its background.", "The largest text is too faint against its background.", "The headline is not much larger than the body text.", "The headline is not set heavier than the body text.", "The space between groups is no bigger than the space inside them.", "Is the logo or site name in the top-left (or top-center) of the screen?", "Is the main navigation one row at the top or one column down the left side?", "Does the main navigation have 7 or fewer top-level items?", "Is there a search box, log-in, sign-up or cart control in the top-right quarter?", "Does the layout follow the usual pattern for its own screen kind (marketing page: headline + one button + proof; app screen: title + grouped controls; modal: title + message + actions; fragment: aligned, evenly spaced items)?", "Do nav and button labels use common words or the company\'s own product names (Log in, Pricing, Contact, Cart, Search, Mac, iPad)?", "Is the page free of unusual patterns (rotated text, hidden or icon-only nav, custom scroll, text on busy images)?", "Too many text sizes are in use.", "Do the text colors use 3 or fewer different hues (greys and black/white do not count)?", "The screen shows a lot of words.", "Some lines of text run long.", "Many boxed panels crowd the screen.", "Some text sits on a gradient or photo.", "Some text is much smaller than the body text.", "The body text is tiny next to the headline.", "More than one button competes as the main action.", "Is the primary button label 1-4 words and does it start with a verb?", "The main button is not visible without scrolling.", "Are there 7 or fewer nav items visible at once?", "Are there 15 or fewer clickable things on the whole screen?", "The headline does not say plainly what the product does.", "Some links or buttons do not look clickable.", "A banner or pop-up next to the main button competes with it.", "Some button labels are generic.", "The sentences run long.", "Is a company name or logo shown at the top?", "The page shows no proof such as customer logos, ratings or user counts.", "The page does not show the real product in use or a real person.", "Is there a contact, privacy, terms, address or phone link visible?", "A promo banner or pop-up competes with the page.", "Is the screen free of broken images, overlapping text or cut-off words?", "Do same-kind items look the same (all buttons one shape and style, all headings one font)?", "Is the copy free of vague filler (world-class, cutting-edge, seamless, empower, solutions)?", "Does the page look professionally designed (clean, current, not archaic)?", "Is the copy free of hype and superlatives (best ever, !!, guaranteed, amazing, shouted all-caps lines)?", "Is the tone plain and confident, with no hedging (maybe, perhaps, we think, kind of)?", "Is the text free of typos and doubled words?", "Is the copy free of pressure tactics (act now, last chance, only 3 left, countdowns)?", "Does the copy sound human but professional (not stiff or corporate, not slangy)?", "Is the background restrained: light, or dark with a calm palette (few hues, no vivid accent)?", "Do cool colors (blue, green, teal, purple) or neutrals make up most of the colored area?", "Does empty space surround the main headline on at least two sides?", "Are there more than 4 different text/accent colors on screen?", "Is the page background near-black with a clashing palette (many hues or a vivid accent)?", "Is the most-used accent color vivid (bright, fully saturated)?", "Is the most-used accent color vivid (bright, fully saturated) rather than muted or pastel?", "Are there 4 or more separate colored blocks competing for attention?", "Is there a full-width gradient, or a large (over a quarter of the screen) multicolor image or ribbon?", "Is the page mostly one hue family plus neutrals (grays, white, black)?", "Is the saturation of the largest colored area muted or pastel?", "Does more than 40 percent of the screen stay empty (no text, image or color)?", "Are all headline weights regular or medium and no text is larger than 3 times body size?", "Is the page background dark (darker colors raise arousal)?", "Does any headline or button name a benefit gained (save, grow, simple, free, easy, clear)?", "Do at least 3 words in the copy come from a positive list (love, simple, easy, free, better, great, clear, fast, joy, welcome)?", "Is the tone welcoming (greeting, thanks, or an offer with no cost)?", "Does any copy name a loss, risk, or danger (lose, risk, miss out, warning, never, kill, danger, error)?", "Does any copy use a negation (\'don\'t\', \'no\', \'not\', \'never\') in the headline?", "Does any copy include a pressure phrase (last chance, hurry, ends, only X left, final)?", "Is the copy free of any feeling word at all (only names, nav labels, prices, specs)?", "Is there at least one exclamation mark in the copy?", "Is any headline or button written in ALL CAPS (more than 2 words)?", "Does any copy use urgency words (now, today, instantly, limited, last, fast)?", "Does any copy use a superlative or extreme word (best, #1, ultimate, never before, revolutionary, 10x)?", "Is the copy all sentence-case, with no exclamation and no urgency word?", "Does the headline use a hedge or soft verb (can, may, helps, supports, gently)?", "Is the copy free of numbers, percentages and big claims?", "Does the screen use 2 or fewer typefaces?", "Is the colour palette limited to one or two accent colours on neutrals?"]
